          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To subtract two fractions with like denominators, we subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same. Therefore,\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{23}{9} - \\dfrac{8}{9} = \\dfrac{23 - 8}{9} = \\dfrac{15}{9}.]</span></p><p>We can simplify this fraction by dividing the numerator and the denominator by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3{:}]</span>\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{15}{9} = \\dfrac{15 \\div 3}{9 \\div 3} = \\dfrac{5}{3}]</span></p><p>Since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5 \\div 3 = 1 \\, \\textrm{R} \\, 2,]</span> we can write the answer as a mixed number:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{5}{3} = 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}]</span></p><p>Therefore, we conclude that\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{23}{9} - \\dfrac{8}{9} = 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To subtract two fractions with like denominators, we subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same. Therefore,\n[MATH: \\dfrac{23}{9} - \\dfrac{8}{9} = \\dfrac{23 - 8}{9} = \\dfrac{15}{9}.]\n\nWe can simplify this fraction by dividing the numerator and the denominator by [MATH: 3{:}]\n[MATH: \\dfrac{15}{9} = \\dfrac{15 \\div 3}{9 \\div 3} = \\dfrac{5}{3}]\n\nSince [MATH: 5 \\div 3 = 1 \\, \\textrm{R} \\, 2,] we can write the answer as a mixed number:\n[MATH: \\dfrac{5}{3} = 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}]\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n[MATH: \\dfrac{23}{9} - \\dfrac{8}{9} = 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}.]",
            "images": [],
